<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Beveridge Report</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1942">1942</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Beveridge Report, officially <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/social-insurance">Social Insurance</a> and Allied Services, was a British government report written by the economist William Beveridge and published in December 1942. It proposed a comprehensive system of social insurance to attack the five giants of want, disease, ignorance, squalor and idleness, and became the blueprint for the post-war welfare state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/beveridge-report.jpg" alt="Beveridge Report" width="320" height="297" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: British Government · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_Beveridge_D_17134.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
